      },
      "title": "Latency per Output Token (p50 / p95) per Deployment",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le, api_base, litellm_model_name) (rate(litellm_deployment_latency_per_output_token_bucket{api_base!=\"\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{api_base}} {{litellm_model_name}} p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, api_base, litellm_model_name) (rate(litellm_deployment_latency_per_output_token_bucket{api_base!=\"\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{api_base}} {{litellm_model_name}} p95",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The gateway (LiteLLM 1.103.0) divides the time of each successful call to a deployment by the number of output tokens of the call. For a call that is not streamed, the time includes the prompt time, the wait in the Ollama queue and any model load. For a streamed call, the time stops at the first token, so the value does not show the decode speed. A call with no output tokens, such as an embedding, records no value. The buckets are the Prometheus client defaults (5 ms, 10 ms, 25 ms and up), so a quantile is an estimate between two bucket limits."
    },
